invariant: INV-52
file: gcm_avx512_kernel.c
catches: test/avx512-run.sh bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test
builds: bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test
reason: register_mask answers every byte of a register that holds any
  byte of the run, so the bytes past the last whole step load and store
  whole registers: the open reads and hashes up to 63 bytes past its
  ciphertext, and the seal reads past its plaintext and writes past its
  ciphertext. bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test puts each buffer's last byte at a
  page's end before a page with no access, requires the bytes past each
  output to keep their value, and holds the tags to the 128-bit loops'.
  It needs a CPU with what CH_CPU_AVX512 names, or Intel SDE through
  SDE64, which the nightly's test-invariants job installs; without either
  this reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    if (held >= REGISTER_BYTES) {
        return ~(__mmask64)0;
    }
--- new
    if (held > 0) {
        return ~(__mmask64)0;
    }
